          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I seal pavers before or after polymeric sand?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On new pavers, install the polymeric sand first, let it cure, then seal. Most manufacturers ask for at least a day or two of cure time, and some recommend waiting several weeks. Sealing first makes any haze harder to remove and can stop the sand bonding to the paver edges. Choose a sealer listed as compatible with polymeric sand."
