          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most concrete paver projects, the choice comes down to two sands. Techniseal HP NextGel is the pick for driveways and smooth or sealed pavers where haze would be obvious. Alliance Gator Maxx G2 is the most forgiving option for a first DIY patio and the easiest to find. Budget sands like PowerLoc and PermaSand are fine for small foot-traffic areas if you follow the watering steps exactly.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The sand is the smaller part of the job. Check the base, clean the joints to the right depth, compact properly, stop below the chamfer, clean the surface completely and water patiently. Get those steps right, and any of these sands will hold your pavers firmly for years.
          </p>
